<!--
Merged into the image's config.xml (config.d). user_files_path and
format_schema_path point at an empty directory the clickhouse user cannot
write. ClickHouse 25.8's sqlite() table function creates its database file
under user_files before it checks the caller's grant, so Grafana's
read-only user, refused every time, still left one empty file per query,
never removed, until the data volume ran out of inodes and ingest failed
(review round six). A CapnProto or Protobuf output without a schema
(formatRow('CapnProto', 1), FORMAT ProtobufList) writes a generated schema
to a temporary file under format_schemas, and one that fails to generate
leaves it there: the same, about 1,000 files a second (review round seven;
the read-only user's profile also turns that generation off). No hopcorder
query uses either directory. CLICKHOUSE_DO_NOT_CHOWN (docker-compose.yml)
keeps the image's entrypoint from handing /srv to the clickhouse user.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <user_files_path>/srv/</user_files_path>
    <format_schema_path>/srv/</format_schema_path>
</clickhouse>
